SPEC = {'file': 'cover_cube_data_analyst', 'label': 'CUBE Data Analyst', 'center': True, 'paras': ["I am writing to apply for the Data Analyst position in CUBE's Customer Data Operations team in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I have actually done: using Python to clean, connect and structure messy data, and automating the repetitive steps so the work is faster and more consistent.", 'What attracts me most to CUBE is the combination of AI and regulatory intelligence. Compliance data is only useful if it is accurate and consistent, and I like that the role involves improving the workflows and tools behind that data, not only running them. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality. I also turned more than 4,800 unstructured patient consultation threads into structured data with a regex and LLM extraction pipeline.', "On working with subject matter experts, much of my experience has been exactly that. At Ipsos Strategy3 I built a coding framework that turned more than 80 healthcare professional interviews into quantitative variables, and at DS Digital I agreed the evaluation rules with the client's clinical experts before building anything. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code.", "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my Python, SQL and automation experience could contribute to CUBE's Customer Data Operations team. I am based in London. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship."]}
